{
  "id": 291913195,
  "iid": 15023,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "JSON-3GPP: Handle 5GC over HTTP/1.1 (OAI), don't create HTTP/2 sessions",
  "description": "http2_get_header_value currently, by calling get_http2_session,\nalways creates HTTP/2 conversation data on the current conversation.\nThis confuses the HTTP dissector if HTTP/2 is not actually present,\nso guard it with proto_is_frame_protocol.\n\nAlso, despite 3GPP TS 29.500 saying that the service based interfaces\nuse HTTP/2 only, OAI (and perhaps other implementations) have options\nto use HTTP/1.1, so try to handle that case as well.\n\nFix #19723",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-03-28T23:52:50.845Z",
  "updated_at": "2024-03-29T14:17:01.642Z",
